WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.167
Late last night, Twitter's

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.802
owner and chief

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.137
twit Elon Musk said

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.172
that Trump, who has been banned since

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.240
inciting an insurrection

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:07.841
at the Capitol

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:08.775
on January 6th,

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.611
is now back on the platform.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.413
Let us discuss all of this

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.515
and more with CNN's Nia-Malika Henderson.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.384
Jonathan Swan of Axios,

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.486
Margaret Talev of Axios, and CNN's

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.955
Manu Raju.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.990
It feels like deja vu a little bit.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.892
The combination of Trump

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.827
going out there and talking witch hunts,

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.996
but also he's back on Twitter

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.865
What will that mean

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.901
for him, for our politics

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.336
this time around?

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.671
Is he back on Twitter, his Twitter?

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:39.873
Remember, like three days?

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.975
Joe is like three days ago.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.877
It was like, this is my last tweet.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.478
If I knew that was my last tweet,

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.413
I would have done whatever.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.648
Like, I I don't know what this is.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:49.816
I don't know what Twitter is.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.718
I don't know what Elon Musk is doing.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.653
And most Americans don't read Twitter.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.288
Margaret, Margaret is all of us.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.790
We don't know what is going on.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.558
But I mean, the reality is that,

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.593
you know, just listen to Trump.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.028
This is what he said last night

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.663
about whether or not

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.065
he would even be interested in

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.099
coming back to Twitter,

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.736
to social

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.671
is is through the roof.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.306
It's doing phenomenally well.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.107
Truth social

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.475
has been very, very powerful,

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.943
very, very strong.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.144
And I'll be saying that.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.379
But I hear we're getting a big vote

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.781
to also go back on Twitter.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:23.850
I don't see it

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.420
because I don't see any reason for it.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.922
Truth, social media,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.323
if you're wondering, is the other thing

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.858
Americans don't know anything about,

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:32.459
and I think that's

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:33.660
the crux of the matter.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.096
Can he resist this bigger?

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.530
It's a much bigger audience.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.331
On Twitter

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.033
than he ever got on Twitter social.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.768
So no matter what he says here,

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.336
there will always be a temptation

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.638
for Trump to take the bigger megaphone.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.140
Yeah, I've spoken to a few of his aides

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.408
over the last

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.343
several months about this question,

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.244
because when it became clear

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.112
that Elon Musk

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.047
was probably going to buy Twitter,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.381
then the next question was, okay,

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.150
does Trump get back on?

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.619
He's saying publicly he won't do it.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.987
But pretty much everyone

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.589
I talked to thinks that at some point

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.157
he's going to go back on this.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.459
If he if he judges that it's expedient

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.193
and useful to him,

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.094
which he believes it is,

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.729
he thinks it's his voice

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.731
directly to the people, etc., etc..

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.499
Now,

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.134
it's kind of the worst nightmare

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.569
of the Republican leadership on the Hill.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.203
Because, you

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.338
know, and

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.239
members of Congress

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.373
and they have to deal with people

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.808
like Manu

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.909
running up to them saying,

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.711
have you seen Trump's latest tweet?

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:25.411
And they say, no,

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.446
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.615
And they run off down the hall.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.717
So, you know, I don't know.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.751
I don't have any reporting

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.620
that he is going to go back on.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.821
But most people around him

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.457
suspect that that is absolutely right.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.659
That is a concern with social.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.760
Republicans could say

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.028
they didn't see it because it is.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.963
And everyone believes that

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.031
most people did not see it

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.432
because those people did. Yes.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.000
I mean,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.234
but when he tweets, it is right

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.303
in the middle of what people are seeing

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.371
when people are consuming

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.805
what the media is consuming.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:53.439
And then that

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.008
forces Republicans to respond,

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.009
which is what has been

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.043
was such a headache

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.411
during the Trump presidency.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.245
So if we respond,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.446
if he does get involved in this,

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.081
I'm sure he won't have many.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:02.815
There won't be many people

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.384
on Capitol Hill who are happy about this.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:04.551
Yeah.

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.251
I mean, it's been

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.719
it has been such a boon

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:07.487
to Republicans

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.088
that they have not had to deal with this

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.557
on a regular basis.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.591
And I think that we are actually

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.159
entering this

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.494
perfect storm

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.796
for a lot of sort of the establishment.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:17.997
We have a drawn out

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.732
Georgia runoff in a few weeks.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.734
Trump is declared. He's running again.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.337
He's maybe going to be back on Twitter

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:25.905
I feel

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:26.272
like I'm

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.341
hearing a lot more nervousness

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.776
about what this could mean

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.377
in amping up the frustration

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.278
of the American people

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.313
with the kinds of stuff

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.914
that they have twice now.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:35.481
But yeah,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.050
Republicans quite worried

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.052
about this particular in this Georgia

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.853
runoff race is December 6th.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.156
Does Trump insert himself there?

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.123
Because now

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.358
he's obviously run for president

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.360
and people are covering him much more.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.895
Does he get back on Twitter?

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:50.430
It is a different landscape,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:50.897
though, right?

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.765
It's even a different media landscape.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.000
I think one of the big questions

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:54.968
we all have is

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.102
how is if

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.104
he tweets in the way that he used to?

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.273
Does the media sort of do wall

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.908
to wall outrage coverage

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.711
in the way that a lot of us did in

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.646
in the past at this point?

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:07.680
Can he

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.915
I mean, what could he tweet

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.950
that could cause outrage at this point?

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:11.184
Right.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.553
I mean, he fomented an insurrection.

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:14.320
He's been racist.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.121
He's been sexist.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.490
He's been terrible in so many ways.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.258
And it was kind of part

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.259
of the culture there

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.960
that there would be this outrage.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.029
We'll see who he is on Twitter

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.464
and we'll see what the reception is,

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.732
not only from the media,

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:26.966
but but you see the media

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.401
saying we're not going to do this again,

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.736
but starting to do it again.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.170
And you also see Republicans

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.672
saying it's time to move on.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.773
But if you have 16

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.975
Republicans in a GOP primary, guess what?

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:38.111
We're going to be right back and start.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.912
Speaking of deja vu, here we are again.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.614
We have another special counsel

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:44.050
in all of these Trump cases.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:47.420
He is facing so many investigations

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.522
to DOJ, once classified documents,

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:50.623
January six.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:51.824
But then there is also

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.026
the January 6th select committee,

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.694
which is on its way out the door,

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.562
the Georgia investigation,

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:57.630
which a lot of people say

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.732
might be his biggest problem.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.701
The House Ways and Means tax probe.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:02.902
The Manhattan D.A.

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:05.505
is on his case, and the New York A.G.

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:06.839
is also

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:09.776
investigating his companies for fraud.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:13.112
There's a lot going on that is

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.048
looming on the horizon for Trump.

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:15.648
Will it matter?

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:17.884
I mean, if he

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.252
gets indicted,

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.788
surely it's hard to game out.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.523
And you know,

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:23.956
especially in

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.725
this Republican primary electorate,

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.360
you don't want to make sweeping

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.728
predictions about what

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:31.097
an indictment might do to

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:31.698
Donald Trump's

00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:33.099
approval rating among public

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.200
and private voters.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.335
There's probably a few, though,

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.936
who won't love it.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.371
Probably a few voters who think

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:40.740
probably not. Great. Just just a few.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.140
Yeah.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:41.641
So Donald

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.675
Trump sees

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:43.376
the special counsel

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.877
through the lens of his

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:45.712
personal experience

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:46.512
with the special counsel,

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.880
which was with Robert Mueller,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.217
which he saw as this unending witch hunt.

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:54.020
So while most people expected this

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:54.887
to happen, Trump

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.422
views it through that lens.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.157
He's been told by his advisers

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.592
that being a

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.393
presidential candidate

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.895
does not immunize him from indictment.

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.865
But I've been told by people close to him

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:06.933
that he still sees it

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.768
as politically advantageous

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:10.370
sorry, legally

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.105
advantageous to be alive

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:13.172
political candidate

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.075
in this context.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.710
He's following the same playbook

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.278
as he did with Mueller saying, you know,

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.546
this is a witch ongoing

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.148
and left wing prosecutor

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.850
or even like this.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.852
Jackson was a career prosecutor

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:27.487
at the Justice Department.

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:29.155
But the difference between Mueller

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:29.822
and now remember,

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:30.990
he was a president then.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:31.324
The reason

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:33.493
why Mueller did not come to a conclusion

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:34.360
and say there was

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.495
he should be prosecuted

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.029
on the issue of obstruction

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:37.830
to the Mueller report

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.065
because he was bound by Justice

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.266
Department policy

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.567
saying you can't charge

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.468
a sitting president.

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.503
He is not a prisoner anymore.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.971
He could most certainly be charged.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.473
So this is a much different circumstance

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:48.040
for Trump.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.542
He's got a lot of legal exposure.

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:50.476
I mean, he has said

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.678
that he won't partake in it.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.180
I don't know that he has a choice

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.182
in terms of partaking in it,

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:57.049
but he'll certainly use

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.484
this same strategy.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:06:59.152
You know,

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:01.320
I mean, he has taken on so much water

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.488
over these last two weeks,

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:04.524
not only with the sound defeat

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:05.558
of election

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:06.893
deniers, his candidates

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.728
in the midterm election,

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.696
but with this news, he will say,

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:11.998
oh, this is good for him.

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:12.832
And it'll certainly,

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:15.001
I think, by net 30% or

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:17.303
so of the Republican Party to him.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:17.970
But again,

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.039
this is not good for his chance.

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:21.741
Overall, I think the only thing that

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:22.875
the only argument

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:23.476
in any way

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:24.610
that this could be good for him

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.678
is that special

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:26.779
prosecutors often

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:27.480
take a long time

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.614
or get bogged down in things.

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:30.883
But this is someone who's much

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:33.586
whose experience includes war crosses.

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:34.587
Jack, Jack Smith.

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:37.123
Jack Smith, you disappointed

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:39.659
International Criminal

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:40.960
Court at The Hague

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.361
War Crimes Investigations

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.463
and prosecutions

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:44.530
and public corruption

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.632
cases back in the U.S., including

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.701
against police officers gone rogue.

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:49.836
So this is someone who

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.737
is not going to be politically

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.005
bound up in any of this

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:53.773
or worrying about it

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.842
and has a tremendous amount of

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:56.943
broad experience

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:59.545
and understands the imperative

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.047
to move swiftly.

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:01.881
And, of course,

00:08:01.881 --> 00:08:03.115
I mean, the American people

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:04.650
play a role in all of this.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.685
Again,

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:08.888
Trump lost the last time around in part

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:10.456
because people

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.058
are kind of sick of the chaos

00:08:12.058 --> 00:08:12.692
and it feels like

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:13.826
we are about to be

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.228
in a brew

00:08:15.228 --> 00:08:16.062
of more chaos

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:17.730
for at least the next two years.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.065
And of course, the question is

00:08:19.065 --> 00:08:20.533
will Republican primary voters

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:21.267
agree with that

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:22.268
or are they tired of the chaos?

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:23.302
Do they want to move on?

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.071
That's going to be the first question.

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:26.205
It will also be interesting to see

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:28.608
whether Trump's allies on the Hill

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:31.644
echo his claims of being a victim of

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:32.778
the witch hunt here.

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:34.347
Do they go after the special constantly?

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:35.781
So some of that from the House

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:36.449
Judiciary Committee.

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:39.151
Republicans are attacking him on Friday.

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.086
A lot of them were saying

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:41.420
there should be a special counsel.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.055
The Hunter Biden investigation

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:43.956
that's happening right now

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:45.124
in the Justice Department.

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.325
So are seeing some of that.

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:48.327
But will they go along with his playbook

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:49.896
and demonizing the special counsel?

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:51.230
Oh, they keep an open mind

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.598
because this is a serious investigation.

